p <em>Verb reduplication</em> is the process in which usually a one-syllable verb is repeated to indicate the brevity or limited scope of the action.

examples

example #[你 nǐ] #1[看看 "kan4 kan4"] 。
trl *1[Have a look].

example #1[说说 "shuō shuō"] #2[你的 "ni de"] #3[想法 xiǎngfǎ] 。
trl *1[Talk a little bit about] *2[your] *3[opinion].

example #1[我 wǒ] #2[想 xiǎng] #3[出去 chūqù] #4[走走 "zǒu zǒu"] 。
trl *1[I] *4[kind of] *2[want to] *3[go] *4[for a walk].

end examples

p The character #[一 yi1] can be inserted between the two instances of the verb.

examples

example #1[我 wǒ] #2[可以 kěyǐ] #3[用 yòng] #3[一 yī] #3[用 yòng] #4[你的 "ni de"] #5[电话 diànhuà] #[吗 ma] ？
trl *2[Can] *1[I] *3[use] *4[your] *5[phone] *3[just a minute]?

end examples